I removed anthropic.claude-opus-4-7 from Bedrock's model list. Every Claude id still on that list now has a preset in yoagent, and a new test enforces that. The commit is 08f0ff2c and carries "Fixes #1121". Clippy, fmt and the full test suite pass (7,570 tests, 0 failed).

What changed
• The list (`src/providers.rs`): opus-4-7 is replaced by anthropic.claude-opus-5-5. I took that id from yoagent's own Bedrock id table, and the new test confirms it resolves to a preset. If someone types opus-4-7 by hand, it still runs. They get the "Unknown model" and "guessed limits" warnings, which are accurate for that id.
• New test (`every_listed_bedrock_claude_id_resolves_a_yoagent_bedrock_preset`): every anthropic. id on the Bedrock list must have a yoagent Bedrock preset and must not trigger the guessed-limits warning. The two Amazon Nova ids are exempt by name, because yoagent has no preset for them and their warning is correct. Any other vendor added to the list fails the test until someone writes a rule for it.
• Renamed test: the old assertion that the list includes opus-4-7 is now test_bedrock_known_models_offer_a_preset_backed_opus_not_opus_4_7. Its doc comment says why the expectation flipped.

Why the existing check missed it: the older test counts an id as known if yoagent has a price for it. yoagent prices opus-4-7 but has no preset for it, on either Anthropic or Bedrock. I first got this wrong too: my comparison case assumed opus-4-7 had an Anthropic preset, and the test failed on that. The comparison case now checks what is actually true: opus-4-7 passes the old check and fails the new one.

Checks
• Re-adding opus-4-7: I put it back on the list with a NEUTERED marker (count 1). The new test failed and named it: "bedrock list offers anthropic.claude-opus-4-7, which has no yoagent Bedrock preset". After I removed it again the marker count was 0 and the test passed.
• Running the built binary against a dead local address:

| id | guessed-limits warning | unknown-model warning |
|---|---|---|
| sonnet-4-6 | none | none |
| opus-5-5 | none | none |
| haiku-4-5 | none | none |
| opus-4-7 (typed by hand) | yes | yes |

Left as is
• KNOWN_MODELS in src/commands.rs keeps claude-opus-4-7. That's the direct Anthropic id in /model tab completion, not a Bedrock id.
• The other #1121 references in the source and docs describe past changes, so they stay accurate after the issue closes.

I posted the results on #1121. I also commented on #1148 that its item 2 (yoagent mapping opus-4-7 on Bedrock) now only matters for people who type that id themselves.
